{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1510727-flux-talents-vs-flux-aberrants-fight","id":1510727,"title":"Flux (Talents) vs. Flux (Aberrants) - FIGHT!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-04T15:53:53-07:00","id":1510727,"title":"Flux (Talents) vs. Flux (Aberrants) - FIGHT!","content":"I'm trying to fit together some metaphysics rules for my understanding as a GM and so I can keep my worldbuilding consistent, and looking for thoughts/input from others.<br /> <br /> Core Trinity describes Flux Storms and other events as a source of Inspiration, or at least a catalyst for future Inspiration, in select individuals. This suggests that a certain environmental element can be applied to Flux allowing for fields/particles/infusions/etc. and that Talents are at their best when Flux is present. The state of the world in Trinity Core also suggests that these storms or environmental manifestations of Flux are not at all damaging to baseline humans or biological life.<br /> <br /> Moving to Aeon we read about Quantum Flux Zones, and their mutagenic and damaging properties. This is literal fallout from the Novas, their byproducts when they couldn't hold it together or when they willingly just went full Godzilla. And any Psion or Baseline that encounters these zones is in for a Bad Day. But what about Talents? Are Talents going to find themselves overwhelmed and have their gifts go haywire? Are they going to get supercharged because this is Flux in a concentration that is &quot;Toxic&quot;, and face some kind of burnout? Or can they stride through like the Winners they are, not even a stubbed toe on the debris?<br /> <br /> I've looked through the books published so far and there is acknowledgment of the parallel terms used, but no talk about delving into the nature of Flux from the core perspective. And maybe that's so GMs like me can tinker with it to our hearts content, but still... what happens when a Talent clashes with Quantum Flux from a Nova?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27972-gm-janus","name":"GM Janus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T16:24:50-07:00","id":1510731,"title":"","content":"It's possible that the result is Aether, or something like it. <b>TC: Aether</b>'s Setting Secrets outright states that <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">the reason why the 19th century got flooded with Aether was because the Martians used Quantum and Talent-style Flux in conjunction; and the result put reality through a figurative meat grinder, with Aether being the resulting ground meat.</div></div> </div> </div> So it wouldn't surprise me if a Talent in a Flux Zone might be at risk of turning into a Magog. <br /> <br /> I'd also have some difficulty making a distinction between a Magog and a sub-aberrant. Both suffer mutations that both give them powers and make them less human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T17:13:47-07:00","id":1510737,"title":"","content":"Iiiiiiinteresting. This is making me look forward to the Aether release even more (I do so love pouring over lore minutia).<br /> <br /> So a follow-up thought is &quot;What would a Quantakinetic see in this cosmic quantum mess?&quot; Likely something akin to the Color Out of Space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27972-gm-janus","name":"GM Janus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T03:03:19-07:00","id":1510768,"title":"","content":"In a certain way a Magog is a Sub-Aberrant with more precise, maybe even studied, way to deal with their mutations and powers. Want it or not, a Magog has some control of the amount of Aether they were receiving, while a Sub-Ab is force feed on quantum.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of Corruption being Aether, or Aether-like, make me think about possibilities\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T03:23:21-07:00","id":1510769,"title":"","content":"Yeah; that's why I cringe whenever someone suggests that high-powered Talents would be \u201clike Magogs, but without the Deviations\u201d. Gogs and Magogs are empowered by what amounts to a blending of Talent-style Flux and Aberrant-style Flux; and both what they can do and what is done to them as a result owe at least as much to the Quantum-adjacent nature of the latter as to the former. Strip away the thing that causes the Deviations, and you also strip away most of what allows Magog Gifts to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T05:14:10-07:00","id":1510773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1510727-flux-talents-vs-flux-aberrants-fight?p=1510769#post1510769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strip away the thing that causes the Deviations, and you also strip away most of what allows Magog Gifts to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely! I understand why people what to have \u201cFree of Corruption Magogs\u201d but then you have a point where Talents become low level (or even quite powerful) Novas.<br /> <br /> Personally I am ok with Talents doing strange things and all, but gaining scale as easily as (or even easier than) a Nova is not on my list of Talent capacities. For example, TBTA gift and other feats of super human skill are very much what Talents should do, but it must require a lot of dedication of the talent, not something a initial Talent should be doing, specially without first understanding what they are dealing with (as most talents deal with their gifts). Assassins, due to their understand of the workings of their powers are more capable, but yet not full novas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T14:35:39-07:00","id":1510920,"title":"","content":"My personal take on defining things thusfar for any players needing definitions;<br /> <br /> Talent = Stunts and abilities you would expect to see in any James Bond, Fast &amp; the Furious, Oceans Eleven, or Indiana Jones movie. If you want to throw fireballs I am going to need a damn good reason.<br /> Nova = Overdramatic DC Comics movies, The Boys, Percy Jackson, or Star Wars Jedi/Sith. If you want to be subtle and blend into a crowd, I am going to need a damn good reason.<br /> Psion = Marvel TV Series, Push (underrated 2009 movie), Captain Planet &amp; The Planeteers, or Mystery Men. Be ready to be good in just one area of power, and if you want to act like a Lone Wolf I am going to need a damn good reason.<br /> <br /> I have yet to get my hands on the Aether material, and my Adventure! pdf is in processing from the TC Players Guide kickstarter. but if I am following the discussion it sounds like Aether is looking to treat the &quot;Price of Power&quot; as a very internalized conflict without the spillover Flux has in Aberrant/Aeon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27972-gm-janus","name":"GM Janus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T17:12:37-07:00","id":1510931,"title":"","content":"Aether is what happens when Flux gets crazy and Talents become capable of opening portals to other places and times (including other realities) and to undo reality changes. We have 3 kinds of characters and they are all variations of Talents, most are just regular talents with this few tricks available for environmental reasons, than we have guys that use technology to guide their powers, more like doctor who using the screw driver than properly inventors, and the last kind that are capable of using this special tricks and much more directly from their powers, but at a certain cost, that can be almost anything, monstrous more often.<br /> <br /> We know they are all Talents because you can start as one and turn to the others due to diverse reasons, like trying to do your tricks without your equipment or being bitten by a contagious monster.<br /> <br /> The rest you can probably guess from the talk, but it\u2019s mostly speculations from our part, overthinking some basic ideas from the secret chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 05-06-2023, 08:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T17:51:16-07:00","id":1510939,"title":"","content":"Interesting. So I'm assuming Anima will pull back a bit since it is cyberspace centric in it's marketing material and explore some kind of inner mind thing against the backdrop of post-AbWar but pre Biotech. Anyone know if this is accurate? Is it known if Flux is playing a part here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27972-gm-janus","name":"GM Janus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T23:16:53-07:00","id":1510958,"title":"","content":"The protagonists of Anima are Talents, in much the same way the protagonists of the core book's setting are Talents: Flux plays the role of allowing the protagonists be larger than life, but doesn't provide any superhuman powers. To the extent that there are special superhuman powers in the setting, they come in the form of bionics (cyborgs are very definitely a thing in the setting) and Glass (the cybernetic brain implant that allows for direct neural interface with the digital world). Well, that and the LitRPG-like digital world that everyone's assumed to be plugged into, which is essentially a fantasy MMORPG: think \u201cSword Art Online\u201d. <br /> <br /> The \u201cinner mind\u201d thing being explored comes from the way Glass is capable of messing with the person's mind: on the positive side, it can do a Matrix-like \u201cI know King Fu\u201d thing where skills that are useful in the physical world can be downloaded directly into your brain; on the negative side, your sense of your identity can be messed with, and potentially even completely overwritten in such a way as to turn you into a completely different person. That latter issue turns out to be a major problem that leads to a crisis amounting to a digital invasion of the Earth; and that, in turn, leads to the eventual banning of Glass-like technologies, explaining why you don't find that sort of thing in the \u00c6on setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}